00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Every city has a breaking point.

2
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
1992 is a crime, thriller, action film directed by Ariel Vromen.

3
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
In 1992, Mercer is desperately trying to rebuild his life and his relationship with his son
amidst the turbulent Los Angeles uprising following the Rodney King verdict.

4
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Across town, another father and son put their own strained relationship to the test as they plot a dangerous heist
to steal catalytic converters, which contain valuable platinum from the factory where Mercer works.

5
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
As tensions rise and chaos erupts, both families reach their
boiling points when their worlds collide.

6
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Mercer, played by Tyrese Gibson.

7
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Riggin Bigby, played by Scott Eastwood.

8
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Lowell, played by Ray Liotta.

9
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Dennis, played by Dylan Arnold.

10
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Titus, played by Oleg Taktarov.

11
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Copeland, played by Clé Bennett.

12
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
1992 is a 2024 American crime heist thriller film directed by Ariel Vromen
and written by Sascha Penn and Vromen from a story by Penn.

13
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
The film stars Tyrese Gibson, Scott Eastwood, and Ray Liotta.

14
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Producer Dot da Genius makes a cameo appearance in the film as his film debut.

15
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The working title of the film, April 29, 1992, refers to the first night of the 1992 Los Angeles
riots, which is when and where the film is set; the title was later simplified to 1992.

16
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
The film was released in the United States on August 30, 2024.

17
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
It received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $2.9 million worldwide.

18
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
The film explores themes of looting, race politics, street
riots, based on true story, racial tension.

19
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
The tone is intense.
